General doc URL structure

Docs are standard just-the-docs Markdown. A tutorial page lives in its own
folder:

    docs/<area>/<name>/
      <name>.md       # the page that is served
      img/            # images referenced by the page (relative img/... paths)

Per-page frontmatter (title, parent, grand_parent, nav_order, permalink) is
maintained directly in each <name>.md.

Notes:
- Parents/Grandparents for *NEW* pages require manual updates to their `yaml`
  heading in order to properly include the page. Specifically `parent`/
  `grand_parent` (and `has_children: true` on the parent page) must be included.
  See `docs/computing/jetstream2/jetstream2.md`, `docs/computing/computing.md`,
  and `docs/computing/external-sources.md` for details.

Codelab migration (temporary)
-----------------------------

The tutorial pages were converted from Google Codelabs. Two pieces of
scaffolding exist only for that one-time conversion and are slated for removal
once it is merged:

- `codelab-sources/<area>/<name>/` — the original exported Codelab
  (`index.html` + `codelab.json`), kept as a reference.
- `codelab2md.py` — the one-off script that generated the Markdown from those
  sources (requires Python 3). Re-running it:

        python3 codelab2md.py

  is idempotent, but it should not be needed for normal editing — after the
  migration, edit the `.md` pages directly.
